    "### Some Math Stuff for Calculating the Win Probability\n",
    "**Raw Win Probability:**  \n",
    "$$P(Win) = \\frac{N_{Win}}{N_{Total}}$$  \n",
    "Where $N_{Win}$ and $N_{Total}$ are the number of games won in that position for the given colour and the total number of games in that position for the given colour.  \n",
    "This metric can be used at baseline but is probably not very robust as we don't have enough data for this to really be representative for all positions. Instead we can use Bayesian shrinkage with a prior of $\\alpha = \\beta = 1$ representing the prior belief that games have a 50% win rate.  \n",
    "  \n",
    "**Win Probability (Bayesian Shrinkage):**\n",
    "$$E[P(Win) | Data] = \\frac{\\alpha + N_{Wins}}{\\alpha + \\beta + N_{total}}$$"
   ]
